                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If Steam had a neutral rating I would have given it to SkyScrappers since it is not a bad game. \n\nThe biggest problem I had with the game is that it gets boring pretty quickly. This is due to a lack of variety in the game especially with the combat. While the game has two combat buttons, both attacks appear to do pretty much the same things so there isn't a lot of variety in the combat. If the game had more variety in the combat I think the game could have been a lot better.\n\nThe platforming aspects of the game are not bad. The platforming controls work well for the most part. I liked the fact that you could jump higher off debris that was more vertical. The problem is that it feels like you need to either focus on jumping up the building or attacking the other players in any given round since it is too hard to do both. \n\nI had some fun with the game but after about a half hour I was getting tired it. If you are going to play the game I would highly recommend playing against other players instead of the computers since the computer AI is not always the greatest. \n\nIf you generally like these type of games and have some friends you can invite over I think you can have some fun with SkyScrappers. If you find the game in a sale you could do a lot worse.\n\nNote: I received a free review copy of the game from the developer.\n\n[url=http://www.geekyhobbies.com/this-weeks-steam-releases-and-reviews-october-16th-2015/#SkyScrappers] Read My Full Review [/url]\n",
